# Keep Docker build contexts small and reproducible.
.git/
.gradle/
**/build/
**/bin/
**/out/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
node_modules/
.next/
.terraform/
*.tfstate*
.env
*.env
!.env.example
**/data/
docs/
load-tests/
!load-tests/build.gradle.kts
# M21.3: same shape as load-tests above — Gradle configures the module on every
# invocation so its build file must be in the context, but no image ever needs its
# source (the services depend on it in test scope only, and this build skips tests).
openapi-tools/
!openapi-tools/build.gradle.kts
# M21.7: and again for the shared test scaffold. Test-scope only, so no image needs
# its source; its build file still has to be here because settings.gradle.kts names it.
test-support/
!test-support/build.gradle.kts
# M22.1: the whole SDK tree. sdks/node and sdks/python are not Gradle projects at all and
# no image has ever needed them; sdks/shared is, so its build file comes back for the same
# configuration-phase reason as the three above.
sdks/
!sdks/shared/build.gradle.kts
README*.md
